    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Write a short, casual cold email from {{ $('Search Params').first().json.agencyName }}, a web and AI/automation agency, to a local business.\n\nAbout the business (a value of '—' means UNKNOWN — treat it as unknown, never as a fact and never as something they lack):\n- Name: {{ $json.name }}\n- City: {{ $json.city }}\n- Website: {{ $json.website }}\n- Rating: {{ $json.rating }} from {{ $json.reviews }} reviews\n- Offers online estimates/booking: {{ $json.onlineEstimates }}\n- Their own listing description: {{ $json.description }}\n- Why we picked them (from our scoring step): {{ $json.reason }}\n\nWrite:\n- subject: short and specific, references them, no clickbait or hype.\n- body: 60 to 90 words, casual and human, first person. Open by referencing a SPECIFIC, TRUE detail from the data above (not generic flattery). One line on what we would set up and the payoff. No hype words, no over-promising.\n\nACCURACY GUARD — this email goes to a real stranger, so every claim must be checkable from the data above:\n- Use ONLY the facts listed above. Never invent history, founding year, family ownership, crew or company size, number of locations, awards, or how long they have been in business.\n- Never assert what the business is NOT doing or does NOT have. In particular: never say they are not running ads, have no website, have no online quotes, or are missing any channel — you were not given that information.\n- Do NOT describe features of their website. You have not seen it.\n- If 'Offers online estimates/booking' is exactly 'yes', do NOT suggest they lack online quotes — write about the follow-up layer behind those requests instead.\n- If 'Offers online estimates/booking' is 'no', you MAY reference the missing online quote path — that one is verified.\n- If the 'why we picked them' line is vague, mentions ads, or names no concrete gap, ignore it and write about what we would set up for them instead of asserting a flaw.\n\nExactly one call to action: {{ $('Search Params').first().json.cta }}\nSign off as {{ $('Search Params').first().json.senderName }} from {{ $('Search Params').first().json.agencyName }}. The body must already include this sign-off. Do not use placeholders like [Name] — use the real details above.",
